From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Patched editions: online, copies meet only copies of the same
 mod

A copy playing a mod's disc and a copy of the release met online as if
they were the same game: the same lobbies, and battles between them,
though the mod changes the game's code and data. A mod's disc now has an
identity, and online play keeps copies apart by it.

- disc_patch::Layer::identity(): the SHA-256 of the patched image's size
  and of each sector the layer lists (its number and contents), in
  order. The same for every copy of the same mod over the same release,
  however it was prepared and whatever the file is called.
- disc_patch::prepare_image(): a disc image a mod already patched,
  compared with the release sector by sector into the same layer as the
  mod's patch gives, so both ways to hand out a mod give one identity
  and the image is no longer needed. A patch or image that changes
  nothing is refused.
- patched::Edition::identity and patched::identity(): the layer's, or
  for a disc image played as it is, a SHA-256 of its size, executable
  and PARAM.SFO (which matches no prepared mod).
- adhoc_version_tag(): the tag a copy logs in with,
  GameProfile::adhoc_version's with "-m" and 12 digits of the identity
  after it (adhoc::ctl::version_tag_with_edition, which shortens the
  port's tag to leave room). Servers that know of tags already keep
  different tags apart, so a modded copy meets only copies of the same
  mod; a copy of the release sends its tag as before.
- Play online's count and the chooser's Play Online say "with this mod".
- psprecomp::Sha256: SHA-256 given a piece at a time.
- portablekit_disc_patch_tests: a made-up mod prepared from a VCDIFF
  patch and from its patched image, both layers read back as the image
  and their identities equal, another mod's different; the version tag
  of a modded copy; the streaming SHA-256.

Verified on Windows: the framework builds (MSVC) and its tests pass,
the new ones included; the ad hoc tests were not run. With Dissidia 012
(ULUS10566) and the Emendatus mod (clang build): its patch and its
patched image prepare into layers of one identity, which a separate
computation from the patched image agrees with; a modded start reports
the tag "<port's tag>-m58fe9ae52cb0"; the release starts as before. Not
verified: a login or a battle with two copies, another game, Linux,
Android.
